<h2>BluHorn</h2>
<p>BluHorn supports media planning and buying workflows, with particular strength in broadcast and local media buying.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Independent agencies that need practical buying workflow without enterprise implementation overhead.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market subscription; confirm current rates with BluHorn.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> More tactical buying workflow; less focused on aggregated market intelligence.</p>
<p><a href="/bluhorn">Learn more about BluHorn on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Camphouse</h2>
<p>Camphouse is a campaign planning and collaboration workspace for media teams.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Teams that need a planning hub, campaign organization, and client-ready workflow.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market to custom depending on team size.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> Lighter planning workspace; not a direct replacement for Guideline's transaction-data intelligence.</p>
<p><a href="/camphouse">Learn more about Camphouse on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Strata</h2>
<p>Strata is an enterprise media buying and operations platform covering planning, activation, billing, and reconciliation.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies needing operational media buying infrastructure.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> Stronger media operations and finance workflow; Guideline is stronger for spend intelligence and MPM data products.</p>
<p><a href="/strata">Learn more about Strata on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>AdLib Planner</h2>
<p>AdLib Planner provides structured media planning and plan-building workflows.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Teams focused on plan development and workflow discipline.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> More planning-centric; less focused on marketplace spend intelligence.</p>
<p><a href="/adlib-planner">Learn more about AdLib Planner on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Mediaocean</h2>
<p>Mediaocean is a large enterprise media management platform spanning workflow, buying, finance, and Prisma digital operations.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Large agencies standardizing media operations across offices and clients.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> More operational system of record; Guideline is more differentiated by transaction intelligence and AI-assisted planning data.</p>
<p><a href="/mediaocean">Learn more about Mediaocean on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Bionic</h2>
<p>Bionic provides media planning, flowcharts, RFPs, and buying workflow for agencies.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies that need structured planning and buying without a heavy enterprise suite.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market to custom depending on seats and modules.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Guideline:</strong> More accessible agency workflow; less market intelligence depth.</p>
<p><a href="/bionic">Learn more about Bionic on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>How to Choose</h2>
<p>Choose Guideline for transaction-backed spend intelligence and enterprise media plan management. Choose Strata or Mediaocean for operational buying infrastructure, Bionic or BluHorn for agency workflow, Camphouse for campaign planning workspace, and AdLib Planner for structured plan building.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is the closest Guideline alternative?</h3>
<p>Mediaocean and Strata are closest for enterprise media workflow. No listed alternative fully replicates Guideline's transaction-data intelligence model.</p>
<h3>Which alternative is best for smaller agencies?</h3>
<p>Bionic, BluHorn, and Camphouse are usually easier to evaluate than enterprise systems.</p>
<h3>Which alternative is best for finance-heavy operations?</h3>
<p>Mediaocean and Strata are stronger fits when buying, billing, reconciliation, and finance workflows are central.</p>
<h3>Do Guideline alternatives publish pricing?</h3>
<p>Mid-market tools may provide more guidance, but most enterprise media management platforms are custom-quoted.</p>
<h3>Can a planning tool replace Guideline's ad intelligence?</h3>
<p>Usually not. Planning workflow tools can replace parts of MPM, but they do not necessarily provide transaction-backed market intelligence.</p>

